NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1090,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,2,4,3,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":4,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.0002,"rank":0.0882,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV000602","role":"target","render":{"description":"Man sees a house on fire and feels that the walls are warm, an omen that the house will burn down.","place":null,"prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/42965","original":"2 Voorloop.\nOp een morgen ging ik naar het werk. \nDaar zag ik opeens het huis van Timp in brand staan.\nNu moet men daar zo snel mogelijk heen gaan.\nZijn de muren koud, dan komt er een dode in dat huis, zijn de muren warm, dan brandt het op.\nIk voelde dus, de muren waren warm.\nDadelijk ging ik naor de vrouw terug.\nIk zeg: \"Timp zien hoes brandt gauw op.\"\nHet heeft nog twee jaar geduurd, toen ging het.","lang":"Standard Dutch; Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV005903","role":"helper","render":{"description":"When his farm burns down, a man says he saw the house on fire long beforehand but kept quiet about it.","place":"Wessingtange","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43264","original":"Veurloop.\nJoarn leden is hier brand west. Ik huilp de boer mit alles. De man stön aal man stil te kiekn en zee:“Nôn brand e ja.”\nIk vruig:“Hou komst door bie, wat betaikent dat?”\n“t Is wol al tien joar leden”, zee e dou, “op n oavend kwam k bie hoes en dou stôn alles in lichtelaaie. k Heb dr nooit over proot, mit ganaine, man nôn brand e ja.”","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.9175,7.14444]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV007406","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Lights are seen as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of fire.","place":"Musselkanaal","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44126","original":"Lichten zaggen ze vrouger voak. \"dr brandt weer wat\", zeden ze, zel wel weer gauw n huus aan goan. Dat geleuf was algemain.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.9325,7.01528]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV013008","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A prediction that all the white houses will burn down comes true; only the white church is still standing.","place":"Bourtange","prov":"Gr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44092","original":"Oal vrouw K. zag vrouger ale widde huuzn in Boertange brannen.\n“Zai brant aal op”, zee ze. En t oal hef nog gliek kreegn ook. Allaind de widde kerke stait dr nog.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.01,7.19028]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Wessingtange.","Find Jipsingboertange on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[52.965,7.10139],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Jipsingboertange"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1936,"rank":0.3801,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ053808","role":"member","render":{"description":"When magpies chatter in the garden by the house, a death is coming. It is an omen.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25423","original":"As eksters op 'e tún by hûs skatterje, dan komt der in sterfgefal.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ064413","role":"member","render":{"description":"Chattering magpies around the house mean that there will soon be a death in that house.","place":"Boelenslaan","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27273","original":"As der eksters om 't hûs hinne skatteren, dat bitsjutte ek, dat der yn dat hûs mei gauwens ien stjerre soe.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ035001","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"At a haunted spot a white lady on a horse used to be seen often. She is a ghost woman.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22709","original":"Op 'e Lytse Wei by de Harkema ried froeger in wite dame op in hynder, doe wie de Lytse Wei noch in sânpaed.\nDurk Pitstra hat har us njonken him hawn op in joun, doe siet er op syn eigen hynder om dat yn 't lân to bringen. Hwat hurder hy ried, hwat hurder dat frommes tasette. Hy koe har net kwyt wurde en dreau op 't lêst yn 't swit.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ026610","role":"member","render":{"description":"In the old days people were afraid when magpies came to the door, because that meant a death.","place":"Boelenslaan","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21410","original":"As der eksters by de doar kommen wienen de minsken froeger bang. Hwant dat bitsjutte in deade.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Harkema belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1391,"rank":0.4477,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ004302","role":"omen","render":{"description":"The narrator's family had heard the hammering on the Malmoune in advance (the Malmoune was a square house for four antisocial families; it was demolished a few years ago).\nThey also heard in advance the sawing and throwing of beams for the house that Sjoerd Stienstra came to live in.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/16068","original":"Wy ha fan tofoaren it timmerjen heard oan 'e Malmoune. (de malmoune wie in fjouwerkant hûs foar fjouwer a-soasiale gesinnen; in pear jier lyn waerd dat hûs ôfbrutsen)\nEk hearden wy fantofoaren it saegjen en 't smiten mei balken fan it hûs dêr't Sjoerd Stienstra, hjir oer de wei, yn kom te wenjen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"Voda_022_16","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A clergyman saw his own funeral. Four men with a bier kept walking behind him all night. He later died on that same road.","place":"Eindhoven","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1977,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/129749","original":"Een geestelijke uit Oirschot zag eens zijn eigen begrafenis. Op een nacht ging hij van Oirschot naar Best. Daar hoorde hij achter zich iemand lopen. Toen ie omkeek, zag ie vier mannen die een baar droegen. Hij wilde wachten, maar toen hie stil bleef staan, bleven ook de dragers stilstaan. En als ie verder ging, gingen ook de dragers verder. Zo bleven deze vier mannen met de baar de gehele nacht achter de geestelijke lopen. Die was blij dat ie eindelijk in Best aankwam, waar hij van de schrik kon bekomen. Enige tijd later moest de geestelijke weer naar Best. Daar stierf hij plotseling. Toen droeg men het lijk van de geestelijke over dezelfde weg die hij gelopen had toen de dragers met de baar hem volgden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ104404","role":"omen","render":{"description":"The evening before IJe shot four policemen dead, the sky already turned red, as a foreshadowing of the blood.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37442","original":"De jouns fan tofoaren foardat de fjouwer plysjes troch IJe Wykstra fan Greategast deasketten waerden wie de loft alhiel read. Dit hat in foarboade west fan it bloedbad.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","4 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":4},"on_success":{"chime":4,"digit":{"value":4,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.6648,"rank":0.5345,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"YPFOE070a","role":"top","render":{"description":"At a crossroads near Jistrum it was haunted at night. One evening, after a party, one of Durk Jaringa's sons passed","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12146","half":"top"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"ZEEUW054","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"There were 3 chests, with a dog on one and on the 2nd a lion holding the key to the 3rd in its mouth, which the man has to take. He does not dare, and the woman takes leave for 100 years.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KEUNING001109","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"notices that at midnight the horse makes a noise, and when she makes a light she sees a woman on the horse.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310F"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"YPFOE070a","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"that crossroads and saw a white figure floating just in front of him. He ran head over heels back to Jistrum. Later some others took him home past the crossroads, but there was no longer anything to be seen of the figure.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ051004","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"As suddenly as the woman and the horse appeared, they vanish again. The man hurries home, scared to death.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"VODA_045_12","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Some have also seen her. But you must not come too close, for then she would pull you into the water.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"ZEEUW056","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The man sees that the dog is the devil and has himself brought back up, after which he is cursed. He comes home ill and stays ill for a long time. He remains poor all his life.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"CJ001413","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He murdered his aunt for her money and since then it has been haunted there. All this happens close to the spot where the house of strong Hearke once stood.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0311"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"ZEEUW053","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The ghost leads him through passages, doors and halls until they come to 5 chests, on which sits a big black dog that takes his breath away. He can no longer speak, and the ghost takes leave for 100 years; the man is back on the road where he was addressed, drags himself home and is dead 2 days later. Someone heard of his adventure and also tried his luck, saw a light dancing ahead of him at midnight, took fright and fled.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"YPFOE088","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"At some point he is fed up with it and wants to wake his brother up properly. In doing so he hits him on the temple, and his brother dies. The family moves away because they can no longer cope. The linden tree has kept on blooming. The murdered boy still haunts the area.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0311"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"KEMP314","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Things would have gone badly for him on any other day. The lady offers him the chance to dig up her money chests, which he may divide between himself, the poor and the church. The next Tuesday Drikus goes with his brother-in-law Hannes to dig up the treasure. But when Hannes says, 'Look, there sits the witch', the chests sink deeper than ever.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"CBOEK305","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"If anyone disturbs her rest, she wrings his neck. A strong man goes to the castle she haunts at night and destroys her for good.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"TINNEV065","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The group starts running. When they have stopped running, the first man tells them he saw a grijze juffer (grey lady).","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310F"},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The top piece breaks off in mid-sentence. The bottom one finishes it.","The number is SINSAG 0310. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c4"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c4"],"stack":["c1","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1405,"rank":0.5773,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"BROUWERS001303","role":"member","render":{"description":"Sighting of a headless woman dressed in white.","place":"Oud-Valkenburg","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"E.H.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131805","original":"Van stropers, -----\nEen zekere S. is hier geweest --- een zekere Joep S. die deed niks anders dan stropen.\nDie heb ik eens horen vertellen dat hij hier achter in het veld, in \"der Maord Gieëlender\" (in 't Moord-Gerendal B [Brouwers]) een vrouw ---- een vrouw recht voor hem uit zag lopen ---- Zonder hoofd, ---- Zonder hoofd. En dat mens liep, hebt U niet gezien.\nJa, of zoiets nu waar is en of zo'n man dat nu maar fantaseert, dat weet ik niet, maar hij vertelde het voor echt.\n ------------\nplaats van handeling: Oud-Valkenburg \n\nvraag opn. : hoe was die vrouw gekleed?\nantw. vert. : zij droeg een lang wit kleed en liep op blote voeten. Maar ze \n zweefde meer als dat ze liep. Zo \n vertelde Joep.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BIJLSMA007508","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Someone with a death's head and glowing eyes walking about at night on hands and feet.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130658","original":"By de Burgemer tsjerke ware nachts in minske op hannen en fuotten om. Hy hie in deadsholle mei eagen as fjûr.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN007503","role":"member","render":{"description":"A headless woman roaming about at night.","place":"Leveroy","prov":"L.","year":1964,"code":null,"initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208804","original":"Vrouw zonder kop. In de buurt van deze boerderij zwierf 's nachts een vrouw rond:\"de vrouw zonder kop\". Iedereen had schrik daarvoor en 's avonds waagde zich niemand in deze omgeving.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"EGGEN001705","role":"member","render":{"description":"Meeting a white woman floating through the air.","place":"Berg","prov":"L.","year":1970,"code":null,"initials":"C.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/207880","original":"Onderwerp : wit wijf.\nTijd : einde 19de eeuw\nPlaats : Berg.\n\nIch weit noch, tot in daen tiēd mèr 'n paar hoezer in Berg sjtonge. En dao op Bemele aan, al gaar gein.\nOppenen aovend, heldere maon, gein mis of gèt, kaom 'n oud vruike nao hoēs, in Berg.\nMèh zie waor kaom aan 't begin van de grwoatstraot (grote straat), dao huërt zie geroēsj in de buim langs de weeg. Dao waor geine wind, en toch roēsjden 't. Zie kraog al gèt angs, en wol vlot wiejer loupe, pes aan de hoezer.\nMèh zie haet nog kaom eine sjtap gezat, dao kump 'n wit wiēf aangezwaef door de loch, zwoa grwoat wie 'ne wollek. \nZie ging rech-op van den angs.\nDoe die versjiening euver waor, leep dat auw minsjke wat 't loupe kòs, nao 't iërsjte hoēs.\nEn van dao haet me hör nao hoēs gebrach.","lang":"Limburgish","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Burgum belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0365,"rank":0.4746,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST283","role":"card","render":{"description":"A minister has to walk home late in the evening through a dark wood. He has a fearful premonition that something will happen to him. And indeed, a wit wief (white woman) shows herself to him. The minister tells the figure that it may stay if it was sent by God, but must leave if it was sent by the devil. The apparition vanishes at once.","place":"Ede","prov":"Gld.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"L.C.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13627","original":"Witte Wieven\nDominee Detmar, te Ede, kwam laat terug van het bezoek bij een ouderling en moest de Witte Wieven bij Kernhem passeren. Hij voelde zich ongerust, er zou hem iets gebeuren. Toch ging hij. Op het Hooge Dennenboschje verscheen hem een witte juffer. Dominee zei: \"Ben je van God, dan staat, ben je van de duivel, dan gaat.\" En de gedaante verdween.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEUNING007301","role":"card","render":{"description":"Sighting of a woman dressed in white who steps over a ditch, crosses in front of a horse and walks on.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310F","initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131331","original":"Pake en omke rieden mei de wein de Achterwei efter de bosk lâns. Doe seach pake in frou oer it lân kommen. Hja wie hielendal yn it wyt. \"Sjoch,\" sei pake tsjin omke. Mar omke seach neat. Pake seach, hoe de frou samar oer de sleat stapte, foar it hynder lâns oer de gong en oer it lân oan de oare kant roun.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ124006","role":"card","render":{"description":"At a haunted spot witte wieven (white women) dance at night.","place":"Mûnein","prov":"Fr.","year":1979,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/32288","original":"Oan 'e dyk to Readtsjerk spûken wite wiven, nei't se seinen. Dy dounsen dêr nachts om.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KOOIJMAN2452","role":"card","render":{"description":"You could see a white lady floating near the Kleine Weeltje.","place":"De Moer","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/127820","original":"Vroeger was er bij ons het Kleine Weeltje. Het bestaat nog, het ligt tussen Klundert en Zevenbergen. Als 't nou goed weer was geweest dan zag je daar op een zomeravond volgens de verhalen een witte dame zweven. Vooral als 't mistig was, als er dauw was. 't Was een wezen met vleugels, ze had helderwitte kleding en een krans om het hoofd. 't Was een glinsterend wezen. Op zomeravonden, dan speelde en vloog ze boven die weel. 't Hoefde niet donker te zijn. En ineens was ze dan weer verdwenen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"LYST277","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand passes the Witte Wieven (white women) and challenges them. One of them chases him all the way home. He just manages to flee inside. But she throws a club at the door, breaking off a piece of the stiepel (doorpost).","place":"Almelo","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"A.G.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13621","original":"In Almelo gaat onder oudere personen (70 - 80 jaar) het verhaal rond van de Witte Wieve van de Alberger hei. Zij vertellen het volgende:\nAlbergen is een gehucht op zes kilometer afstand van Almelo aan de weg naar Ootmarsum. De Alberger hei strekte zich vroeger uit tussen dit gehucht en de bezittingen van Huize Almelo. Men dacht dat ze woonden in een grote tumulus, die zich in 't midden bevond. Men zegt dan, dat als voorzorgsmaatregel, dat de witte wieve niet in huis zouden komen, de boerenbehuizingen een kruis in de middenpost van de baanderdeur, \"stiepel\" genaamd, hadden aangebracht op ongeveer een meter. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ057303","role":"sill","render":{"description":"Several people have seen two witte wijven (white women) in the woods.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25852","stain":"two"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with O.","Opende. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c6","object":"window","text":"Opende"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c6","word":"two","stained":"c6"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P6","difficulty":3.3045,"rank":0.8837,"note":"Each story one number. In this order.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"YPFOE114a","role":"clip1","render":{"description":"One story about werewolves goes as follows: a man and a woman come driving up in a carriage. The man calls to his wife several times that she must let him out. He warns her that otherwise something terrible will happen to her. The woman becomes frightened and lets him out of the carriage. She drives on quickly, but the man flies after her. She only just manages to escape.","place":"Leeuwarden","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":null,"initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12467","original":"Wjerwolven\nSa haw ik yn myn jonge jierren wol ris heard fan wat se dan neamden de wjerwolf. En dat skynde dan noch al ris foar te kommen. Ien ferhaal wisten se my foar wier te fertellen, dat is bard yn'e Hommerts.\nDêr kaam in pearke oanriden op in krompanelen seas. Se rieden op nei hûs en op in stuit sei de feint tsjin 'e faam: 'Do moatst der my út litte! Do moatst der my út litte!' 'Wêrom dat?''Oars bart der wat dat dy ivich spite sil!'\nNo, en hy hâlde sa oan, dat sy waard bang fan him—ik tink, dat sy mende—en se hâlde it hynder yn en liet him fan 'e seas ôf. Doe ried se wer fuort en nei't it ferhaal dan giet, fleach er har efternei en koe se mar justjes úntkomme.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"GENDT089","role":"clip2","render":{"description":"A group of card players thinks that one of them is a werewolf. When this man wants to leave in the evening, they hold him and do not let him go. When his wolfskin comes down the chimney, it falls into the fire and burns. Now the man is freed.","place":"Gendt","prov":"Gld.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"M.H.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/49725","original":"Mien voader het wel es verteld, dat ze vroeger duk same gienge koarte, erges bé’j iemes ien de buurt. D’r waster één ien de ploeg, wor ze van dochte, dattie duk gieng werwolve. Op ’n keer ware ze weer on ’t koarte. Op zekere tied wou die kjel weg. Mar d’aander wouwe ’m nie loate goan. Ze hemmen ’m vasgegrope en ’m nie losgeloate, al gieng ie nog zo d’rop. Opens kwam er ’n wolvevel dör de schorsten valle. Da verbraandde. En toe zeitie: “Nou ziet ’k teraf! As ik los gekomme was en ik had ’t vel kunne kriege, dan ha’k hier alles kort en klein geslage”.","lang":"Gendt dialect (Achterhoek)","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ085401","role":"clip3","render":{"description":"One of seven brothers is a werewolf. When he has one of his fits, you must throw him an old apron or something like it. He then tears it to pieces. If you see someone with threads hanging from his mouth, you can be sure he is a werewolf.","place":"Rottevalle","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33002","original":"In wearwolf is in minske, dy forropt de boel. 't Is ien fan sawn jonges (7 bruorren). As er wer sa'n kuer krijt, dat er hwat forskuorre mat, mat men him in âld skelk of sahwathinne tasmite. Us mem sei, dan gebeurde 't wol dat him even letter de triedden ta de mûle úthongen.\nAs men sa'n ien seach, dy't triedden ta de mûle út hie, koe men der fan op oan dat it in wearwolf wie. Dêr koe men se oan herkenne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ZEEUW180","role":"inside","render":{"description":"Werewolves knew their hour when they had to go; when they then came back to their girl, they had red threads from a shawl between their teeth.","place":"Hulst","prov":"Zl.","year":1923,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"P.A.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35896","original":"Weerwolven.\n\nIk 'èn mijn moeder nie lank gekend. Z' is gestorven in 't jaar da'nk mijn êêste kommienie gedaan èn, maar ik weet nog goed de' ze altijd vertelde-n van Ossaart in van wjèrwolven, in wij stongen d'r ammaal rond, in luisteren, da' begrijpte.\nDan vertelde-n ze van die jongers, da' waren wjèrwolven, in die wisten ulder uur, in dan mochten ze weg. An'ze dan bij ulder meid waren Sondaasavens, dan mochten z' in eens weg in dan gebeurde-n 't an 'ze trugkwamen dan de rôôie draaien van 'ne sjal tussen ulder tanden zaten.","lang":"Zeelandic","front":"description","note":"This one I keep apart."},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Each story counts.","The first number is 1.","1 — 1 — 7."],"lock":{"kind":"number3","salt":"beb94d96b42a8c9d","accepted_hashes":["3744f6259f04196671909050eac3f1b0953d2d9a48fbd5f699dd4bd2defd29f5"]},"on_success":{"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2475,"rank":0.7798,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ015102","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"An impatient, rough farmer wants a large piece of land ploughed before evening. The farmhand refuses and tells the farmer he can take his proposal to the devil. The farmer takes this literally and enlists the devil's help. The next morning the land is ploughed. His dealings with the devil cost the farmer dearly: on his deathbed he was fetched by the devil.","place":"Hurdegaryp","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19770","original":"Der wie in boer, dat wie in forwoesteling. Hy wie altyd gleonhastich en net in arbeider dy't it by him úthâlde koe. Op in kear hied er wer in arbeider, doe moest der ploege wurde. It wie al let yn 'e joun en it wie ûnmooglik dy greate hoeke lân foar de nacht noch to ploeijen. Dat de arbeider sei tsjin 'e boer: \"Freegje de duvel, dat dy it docht.\" De boer sei: \"Dat dog ik\" en hy die it ek.\nDe oare moarns wie it stik lân ploege.\nMar hy hat it sûr bikeapje matten. Doe't er op syn stjerbêd lei, hat de duvel him helle.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"member","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":null,"initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"ENGELS000115","role":"member","render":{"description":"Werewolf leaps on people in the evening; as a helper with work; transformation into a werewolf by putting on a hidden coat, release after the coat is burned.","place":"Helden","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/57969","original":"Weerwolven:\nMannen, die wat laat op de baan waren, werden, vooral in donkere, stormachtige nachten soms besprongen door de weerwolf. Dit spookdier met gloeiende ogen sprong hen op de rug, en klemde zich met de voorpoten om hun nek. Ze bleven zich als een zware last aan de verschrikte man klemmen totdat hij ergens een huis bereikte. In de Broekbeemd, tussen Onder-Eijndt en Zandberg, stond ergens een holle eiken knot of poesjt. Er was een man, die als weerwolf bekend werd. Hij had een aparte jas; als hij deze aantrok werd hij weerwolf. Na zijn nachtelijke tochten verborg hij deze jas in die holle “poesjt”. Zijn buurlui ontdekten dit, en staken de “poesjt” met de jas in brand. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Limburgish","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KEMP298","role":"member","render":{"description":"A tenant farmer finds out that a young shepherd on his farm is probably a werewolf. He sends him away for a day, and he and his farmhands discover a wolfskin in a hollow willow. They set fire to it at home. The shepherd then comes back at a furious pace and tries to grab his skin back. When he fails, the shepherd flees to the hollow tree and is never seen again.","place":"Broek","prov":"L.","year":1925,"code":null,"initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43423","original":"Het weerwolfsvel verbrand\n\nBij de pachter van de boerderij bij het kasteel Geusselt onder Amby diende eens een scheper, een klein manneke, dat de naam had een weerwolf te zijn. 's Nachts was hij nooit in bed te vinden, maar 's morgens lag hij er weer in. De knechts van de hoeve hadden dat al dikwijls bemerkt.\nWijl dit zo opvallend was, werd zijn doen en laten gedurig bespied en zo bemerkte men dan ook dat hij, wanneer hij 's avonds uit zijn bed kroop, naar een weide ging, waar heel eenzaam een grote holle wilg stond. Daar verdween hij iedere keer in.\nOm het fijne van de zaak te achterhalen stuurde de pachter hem op zekere namiddag naar een dorp, dat meer dan drie uur van de hoeve lag, om daar koeien te kopen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Hurdegaryp belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.1088,"rank":0.8205,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST008","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every night at exactly twelve o'clock a farmhand takes a small hoop out of the lime tree. He hangs the hoop around his neck and turns into a werewolf. He roams about for a while and tears apart everything that comes near him. After that he becomes an ordinary person again. The farmer finds his behaviour strange and asks the priest for advice. The priest realises that the farmhand is a werewolf and advises the farmer to send the farmhand on an errand from which he can never be back home by midnight. On the agreed night the priest takes the hoop out of the tree at midnight. The farmhand is standing under that tree and sees everything. He flees and never comes back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0803","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13222","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen boerenknecht kroop 's nachts klokslag 12 uur in de lindenboom voor de boerderij. Boven in de boom hing voor gewone mensen onzichtbaar een hoepeltje. Dat hing de knecht om zijn hals. Als ie uit de boom geklauterd was, liep ie in de gedaante van een hond weg en verscheurde alles wat hem in de weg kwam. Als ie een tijd zo rondgelopen had, was ie weer gewoon mens. Na een tijd was het de boer, bij wie de weerwolf in dienst was, opgevallen, dat zijn knecht nacht op nacht weg was. Hij ging naar de pastoor en die had het zaakje meteen door. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST189","role":"door","render":{"description":"Three people tell that late one evening they met a big dog with fiery eyes that jumped on their backs. Only at the edge of the field did it jump off and vanish. The dog vanished near a farm already known as uncanny, because the farmhand there said that the cows several times jumped up at the stroke of midnight while the stable doors flew open by themselves.","place":"Puiflijk","prov":"Gld.","year":1957,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"C.v.d.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13453","original":"Spookdieren\nMij is eens door drie verschillende personen op zeer verschillende tijden meegedeeld dat op de Waaldijk tussen Boven-Leeuwen en Druten 's avonds in pikdonker plotseling een abnormale grote hond, die plotseling verscheen, hen zwijgend met vurige ogen volgde en even plots aan de grens van Druten verdween. Beide personen waren niet bijgelovig maar hadden van angst 't zweet op de rug staan van angst, temeer daar de hond verdween bij een boerderij waar 't niet \"pluis\" scheen te zijn. Een knecht op deze boerderij vertelde mij eens hoe verscheidene malen 's nachts de koeien om klokslag 12 uur opsprongen en staldeuren openvlogen zonder 'n aanwijsbare oorzaak. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"TINNEV042","role":"card","render":{"description":"Two men are looking for grass stalks to cut. When they find none, they go home. After they have parted, one of the men suddenly sees a large wolf on his path. The next morning the other man asks him whether he saw the wolf.","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1944,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.T.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22388","original":"29.\nPeter ging op een kier met Dorus mieskes sni'je. Mao zi'j konne de gin vinne en wolle daorum weer op huus aan. De weg liep deur een buske. Dorus vroeg aan Peter offe um nao huus sol brenge. \"Loop nao da galg\", antwore Peter en kroap onder de scheibeum nève de weg hèèr.\n\"Hi'j is ter\", riep Dorus um nao. Ienéns stong d'r een grote wolf op de bosweg. Hi'j wol niet op zied gaon. Daorum drèèje Peter de met een flinken boag umhen. Toe e is umkek zag e niks meer. Umdat Peter geld neudig had ginge de 's marges weer op uut um smele te zuke. Ien Kilder was Dorus al met een groten trop aan 't sni'je. Toe hi'j Peter zag riep tem toe: \"Wasse d'r now, of niet?\".","lang":"Liemers dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ071510","role":"card","render":{"description":"A werewolf is a young man who rides a horse. He torments the horse just as a nightmare torments a person. He is one of seven brothers.","place":"Rohel","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28067","original":"In wjerwolf is in manspersoan, - meastal in jongkeardel -, dy't op in hynder rydt. Hy pleaget dat hynder, krekt as in nachtmerje de minsken. 't Is ien fan sawn bruorren. Ik ha wol ien kend, dy wenne yn Warffum.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","3 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c2","object":"door","n":3},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c3","c4","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":6,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.696,"rank":0.5,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ012304","role":"variant","render":{"description":"At night a man runs into an exceptionally tall person. The man could not tell whether it was a man or a woman, and the person did not respond to his greeting.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0475","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19313","original":"Us heit is us in kear tsjin ien oanroan op 'e Berchloane hjir yn Drachten. 't Wie yn 'e nacht. Heit woarde bot kjel, mar dy oare hielendal net. It wie ien, dy wie útsûnderlike lang. Heit moest in hiel ein omheech sjen, woed er it gesicht observearje. Heit koe net gewaer wurde of it in man of in frommes wie mar it wie in hiel lang wezen en 't sei neat, doe't heit \"navend\" sei.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ071105","role":"variant","render":{"description":"One evening a young man saw two men pass by. They made no reply to his greeting and suddenly vanished.","place":"Twijzel","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0475","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28005","original":"In jongfeint tsjinne achter de Falom.\nHy reizge op in joun lâns de Boppe-wei mei de Spûkloane nei Kollumersweach.\nDêr kom er twa man tsjin en it like krekt as hienen dy ien tusken har yn.\nHy moest har passeare en sei: \"Goejoun.\"\nMar sy seinen neat werom en wienen samar ynienen fuort.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ087607","role":"variant","render":{"description":"Early one morning a man saw a man on the verge. The stranger made no reply to his greeting. He hurried off, and the man could not catch up with him at all. It seemed as if the stranger was floating; the man could not find any footprints of him either.","place":"Drogeham","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":"SINSAG 0475","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33174","original":"Op in moarn roan ús heit fan 'e Harkema nei 't Wytfean ta. Hy soe nei de boer ta to melken. Underweis soed er syn maet oanhelje. Dy wenne ek yn 'e Harkema en dy arbeide ek by in boer op it Wytfean.\nHeit wie noch net oan dy man ta, doe kom der him ien tomjitte yn 'e berm. Heit sei: Goeije morgen, mar dy oare sei neat werom. Doe sei heit nochris Goeije morgen, mar de oare sei wer neat. Dit is in nuver spul, tocht heit, dêr wol 'k mear fan wite. Heit der achteroan.\nIt mes hie heit ta de bûse út lutsen en dat hâldde er klear. Mar hy koe dy oare net birinne. Dy oare sweefde. Dyselde hie gjin fuotten. Doe't heit sa in ein roan hie, skeat de oare by ien op it hiem en fuort wied er. Heit der achteroan, èk it hiem op. …","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Friesland a time of day was mentioned: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1966.","That card names a time of day. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"beb94d96b42a8c9d","accepted_hashes":["1bb32a6ec4b03f7fadbcd71916e09d2d9e6c2e34bc148cf73b26280bbf87e409","a852e773c08b8f52309d3f48618e669944c1295396d137126d87a39fca557a5e","d5d2fb9b5b007c01cdfdebfffc1a35066d7310d1f9e8da99a8ae43f1116c1b3a","f246ad2d099910767a5c07fd0142de7ce48b0589663eae03bdf5e91c5d2e8a11"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2288,"rank":0.7393,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ025502","role":"member","render":{"description":"In Westereinde two girls always haunt at night.","place":"Kollum","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21287","original":"Yn 'e Westerein, yn in loantsje by 't spoar, roannen yn 'e nacht altyd twa famkes om. Dy spoeken dêr. Dêr doarsten de minsken nachts net lâns.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ093617","role":"member","render":{"description":"In the old days people sometimes saw witte wijven (white women).","place":"Rottevalle","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33731","original":"Yn 'e omkriten fan Rottefalle hâldden froeger wite wiven ta.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ057209","role":"member","render":{"description":"People used to often see a girl in black silk clothes haunting.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25831","original":"Op 'e Mûzewei (= Mûntse-wei) fan Aldwâld nei Feankleaster spoeke in juffer yn 't swart. Dy roan dêr altyd om. Underskate lju ha har dêr sjoen. Hja hie swart-sidene mofkes oan 'e hannen en in swart-sidene jurk hie se oan. Hja gong dêr nei in plaets ta. Dêr stie in plakje mei woartels flak by. Dêr roan se altyd oan ta, dan gong se werom. Guon seinen. hja gong ek wol nei 't slot ta. De minsken hearden de side ritseljen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"HOL001815","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Werewolves wear a skin and make themselves carried; a place where they can be heard.","place":"Lienden","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209954","original":"Weerwolven hadden een vel om. Ze hadden er plezier om bij iemand op de kruiwagen, ook op de rug te springen. Die dit overkwam moest de weerwolf kruien of dragen. En die was zwaar, hoor!\nJuffrouw Van Kalkeren weet nog, hoe haar vader (geb. 1861) altijd blij was geweest, dat hij \"de krump”\"(= de kromming, bocht) van de Groene Straat, waarin hij voor zijn huwelijk woonde, was gepasseerd. In die \"krump\" zaten altijd weerwolven te brommen. (Ik ben na afloop van deze opname door de Groene Straat teruggegaan, terwijl het al donker was en heb geen gebrom gehoord).","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:3"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a werewolf.","The card about Lienden belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.1885,"rank":0.7083,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CBAK0376","role":"top","render":{"description":"A farmer on a haunted farm asks a begging old soldier whether he will keep watch at night.","place":"Uitdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1903,"code":"SINSAG 0401","initials":"C.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/9190","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ081008","role":"half","render":{"description":"There at the roadside they saw a giant, fully twice the size of a normal person. A large cloak flapped around him; otherwise he stood completely still. It was a ghost.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"BIJLSMA003301","role":"half","render":{"description":"After his death his widow hears in the evenings the same sound her husband made when he went upstairs. Visitors go to look and hear knocking at a book. When it is picked up, the papers fall out of the book.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ058107","role":"half","render":{"description":"Suddenly they saw a fellow wearing a hat. When he passed them, he suddenly vanished.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CBAK0513","role":"half","render":{"description":"The answer is that they have waited a long time for someone, that there is money buried of which he may have a third, and the rest must go in equal parts to the poor and a church congregation. Once the request has been carried out, the haunting stops.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ015103","role":"half","render":{"description":"As the man and his new bride are about to get into the carriage, his dead wife suddenly appears. She reminds him of his promise and the newlyweds undo the marriage. The spirit of the dead can only find rest once a promise made before death is kept.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CBAK0376","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"At midnight, after a lot of noise, six high-ranking officers with sabres come in and go to the haystack. There they dig a hole, take out a kettle of gold coins, bury it again and leave. With a farmhand's help the beggar digs up the kettle. The next night they keep watch together and see the men come again, who leave and never come back when they find nothing. The soldier stays on the farm. According to the narrator it was providence that the soldier was meant to have the money.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401","stain":"six"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘farm’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0401. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c7","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c7"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":6,"card":"c1","word":"six","stained":"c7"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
